\section{Mesh Deformation and Jacobian Stress Test}

For each tetrahedron \(T_i\), define the Jacobian determinant
\[
J(T_i) = \det[\mathbf{e}_1, \mathbf{e}_2, \mathbf{e}_3].
\]

Stress testing requires:
\[
J(T_i) \to 0^+ \quad \Rightarrow \quad \text{Delaunay recovery or remeshing},
\]
while preserving
\[
\det(g_{\mu\nu}^{(i)}) > 0, \quad \chi(\mathcal{T}) = \text{const}.
\]